From f0e32e2e1e3dff4292352770b2c16b090bc4da96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senne Cools <113857183+sennecools@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:42:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/33] d3d12_xs: say what is known about slots 25 and 43

AI-assisted.
---
 docs/d3d12_vulkan.md            | 5 +++--
 runtime/shims/d3d12_xs_device.h | 5 +++--
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/d3d12_vulkan.md b/docs/d3d12_vulkan.md
index f2f32638b..ba16a3cdf 100644
--- a/docs/d3d12_vulkan.md
+++ b/docs/d3d12_vulkan.md
@@ -2221,8 +2221,9 @@ The trace will enumerate them.
   RDX, node mask in R8 and heap type in R9: three calls right after device creation, node mask 1 and types 1, 2
   and 3 (measured under `gta6rt --run` with a register probe in the slot's thunk). A PC C++ method has the device
   in RCX and the buffer in RDX, so the Xbox-ABI proxy takes the console form when RDX holds the proxy
-  (`d3d12_xs_device.cpp`; `xs_proxy_mock_test`, `device_proxy_test`). Slots 25 and 43 return structs too; the
-  executable has not been seen calling them yet, so the proxy still forwards them in the PC form.
+  (`d3d12_xs_device.cpp`; `xs_proxy_mock_test`, `device_proxy_test`). Slots 25 and 43 return structs too and the
+  proxy still forwards them in the PC form: slot 25 is reported called the same way later in the boot (#6982),
+  with console resource descriptions that need converting first, and no call of slot 43 has been seen.
 - Residency and power (D3D-33) are no-ops that still check their arguments (`d3d12_vulkan_device.cpp`, tested in
   `d3d12_vulkan_device_test`). Vulkan has no residency API: memory from `vkAllocateMemory` stays usable until
   `vkFreeMemory`, and paging under pressure is the kernel driver's job, so every pageable object is always resident.
diff --git a/runtime/shims/d3d12_xs_device.h b/runtime/shims/d3d12_xs_device.h
index b1b766510..60103f61f 100644
--- a/runtime/shims/d3d12_xs_device.h
+++ b/runtime/shims/d3d12_xs_device.h
@@ -4,8 +4,9 @@
 //   slot 26   GetCustomHeapProperties, the PC slot, but the retail executable calls it with the buffer for the
 //             returned struct in RCX and the device in RDX (node mask in R8, heap type in R9). A PC C++ method has
 //             the device in RCX and the buffer in RDX. The thunk takes the console form when RDX holds a device
-//             proxy, and forwards the PC form otherwise. Slots 25 and 43 return structs too; no call of them by
-//             the executable has been seen yet, so they are forwarded in the PC form.
+//             proxy, and forwards the PC form otherwise. Slots 25 and 43 return structs too and are still
+//             forwarded in the PC form: 25 is reported called the same way later in the boot (#6982), with console
+//             resource descriptions the PC method cannot take as they are, and no call of 43 has been seen.
 //   slot 62   CreateComputePipelineState(desc, w2, w3, iid, out): two words (0 from XboxBvhBuilder, meaning unknown)
 //             before the IID. The PC slot 62 is CreateStateObject.
 //   slot 67   CreateComputePipelineState from native code (desc, iid, out): converts the Xbox native-code desc
